  "description": "In 1990 Vietnam produced less than $100 per person a year and Indonesia almost six times as much. In 2025, for the first time in the World Bank's records, Vietnam passed Indonesia in GDP per person adjusted for prices, and it's now ahead in plain dollars too. How the poorer country won (speed, exports, factories, people), why Indonesia didn't follow (coal, palm oil, nickel), and the twist: Indonesia's economy is still almost three times bigger, far more stable, and poverty there has nearly vanished.\n\nSources: World Bank WDI (NY.GDP.PCAP.PP.CD, NY.GDP.PCAP.CD, NY.GDP.PCAP.PP.KD, NY.GDP.MKTP.KD.ZG, NE.EXP.GNFS.ZS, TX.VAL.MRCH.CD.WT, TX.VAL.TECH.MF.ZS, BX.KLT.DINV.WD.GD.ZS, TX.VAL.FUEL.ZS.UN, TX.VAL.MMTL.ZS.UN, SL.AGR.EMPL.ZS, HD.HCI.OVRL, NY.GDP.MKTP.CD, SI.POV.DDAY, SP.POP.65UP.TO.ZS, SP.DYN.TFRT.IN); USGS Mineral Commodity Summaries 2026 (nickel); Vietnam customs (exports to the US, Jan–Nov 2025).\n{music_credits}\nNarration is AI-generated.\n\n#vietnam #indonesia #asia #economics #data",
